A||||9||86se/lambo||performance question(1fst 2m6)||||14||
Z||000000||86se/lambo||06-18-2000||01:25 AM||||i read in one of the threads about a throttle body coolant bypass..whats that all about? did you have to have your hypertech chip reburned when you went to nitrous? where is the most affordable place to buy the thermomaster chip(already have the fan switch and thermostat)? also i checked my fuel preesure and it was 35 at idle, does that sound low? oh ya last thing, have you (or anyone) messed around with the power pulleys?||||reg||14
Z||000001||HYPTNOTiSE||06-18-2000||01:36 PM||||Great to see that you want to hotrod your car a little!  As far as a chip, DO NOT WASTE YOUR MONEY!  It will no help at all.  If you really must buy a chip, but it for it's features, like no bump in the throttle at 1600rpm, no rev limiter, and no egr operation, dont do it because you think it's going to make your car faster.  As for as throttle body coolant bypass, here's what ya do.  Go to the hardware store with your TB. Look for some metric bolts not sure what size, maybe 12mm or so, that go into the brass ends of your TB, you'll have to shorten them to make the intall look really clean.  Next take the coolant lines off and where they attach to the thermostat housing just put a loop of rubber hose there or weld the extra ports shut.  You'll also have to cut the map sensor bracket off the tubes but it's no big deal.  Power pullys are ok, worth about 3-5hp i think,  heck out <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178</A>  that's my buddy shauns webpage it's got a right up of the power pulley. Check out my page too at Hometown.aol.com/hyptnotise. It's kinda basic just click on any of the pics for more info.  That's all i can think of for now, i cant remember any of the other questions you asked.<P>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 GT with Competition built 3.2 and nitrous||||reg||14
Z||000002||Shaun41178||06-18-2000||03:21 PM||||As far as the chip I have to agree with hyptnotise.  Don't get one.  For the $100 for the Hypertech or what not it doesn't give any performance over the stock one.  I have seen dyno tests first hand.  If you get one and you have a manual tranny get joe Wynmans.  He deletes the egr, and some otehr little things.  People seem to like his chip better and it is cheaper too at like around $50 i think.<P>A chip does not have to be burned to run nitrous.  Stock chip will work fine.  <P>Fuel pressure seems a bit low at 35 psi.  Is that at the rail?  Might be time for a new fuel pump.  How many miles on the car?  If you want a cheaper way of raising fuel pressure go with an adj fuel pressure regulator.  You cna get one for around $70 and can adj pressure so you have 45 or so or whatever you want.<P>Power pulley is on my website that Hyptnotise put a link up to.  i gained a few hp from thi s mod.  I couldnt' feel a difference however but it did make a difference at the track.  You can read about it by clicking on the link  in Hyptnotise's post.  <P>Shaun||||reg||1
Z||000003||1FST2M6||06-18-2000||09:52 PM||||sorry  for not paying attn:...   everyone is right about the chip.. I HAD to have a new one burned cause i have MUCH larger injectors... my car wouldn't run at all with the stock chip and would only run about 2200rpm at part throttle with the ADS Strip chip i had... I now have a custom burned chip from Custom Network Motors. and it is made strickly for NITROUS operation.. it gets about 8mpg and runs like crap when not under nitrous or WOT.  If your looking for a real upgrade... get an MSD 6 (A or AL)  the A will be fine. a decent coil, new wires a REAL coil wire (8mm or larger) and better exhaust. the stock exhaust is CRAPPY! use 2.5" piping or if your going for a TRUE dual set up (saw it on this page i'll post it up in a few minutes) use 2.25" there is enought back pressure in the factory manifolds and y pipe to NOT burn a valve and the larger rest of the exhaust will aid in the quick tach-in' up of the motor. (that what we found) Don't waste you money on headers... unless you have a 3.4, a supercharger, or nitrous. Save your money on the chip.  the throttle body bypass makes a bigger difference in colder weather than when its already 90 outside... let the intake air stay the same temp as the MAT sensor reads.  And make sure your MAT sensor is in good working order.. if its old and rusty odds are the impediance is wrong and its reading that the air is the wrong temp sending the incorrect amount of fuel to the cylinders. over the next month i will be posting a bunch of mods and their HP increase/decrease  to my newly aquired 87 GT from GT Bastard. his car is STOCK. and a GREAT pallet to start on and let everone know what to do and what NOT to waste their time on... the K&N filer for example.. we (Black GT and myself) ran his car on the dyno then installed a K&N.. yes there was a gain about 3-lbft of torque and 1.5hp... not sure if it's worth the $35 for the filter other then you NEVER have to replace it...    thanks to the guys at Engineered Performance for letting us use their Dynojet. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||06-18-2000||11:00 PM||||Well... Stock except for ported head, K&N, MSD coil, ported exhaust manifolds....   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  But other than that, it's like she just drove off the showroom floor.  hehe||||reg||1
Z||000005||86se/lambo||06-19-2000||03:42 AM||||thanks guys for the advice. i'm currently using the 160' t-stat and hypertech fan switch, and it runs well...but iknow it's running rich..kinda scared to look at the plugs. i know it wont pass smog without the chip so i can be in open loop mode. i have the accel coil,ported exhaust manifols, no muffler with resonator tips and a k&n cone filter.I also wrapped the intake tube with heat resistant tape... might not help, but the y pipe is so close i figured why not. the car has 90k and the fuel pressure was 35 at the rail,which vender do you suggest for the regulator? personally i think they can handle a little more fuel because i can FEEL<BR>the difference with the cool intake charge and extra "start up" fuel... of course no dyno results..but i feel i'm at 160 hp..ooh and i like it with that 4-speed.||||reg||10
Z||000006||1FST2M6||06-19-2000||01:12 PM||||JEFF!!  SHHHH! its stock!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><BR>86SE/L, you being in Calif. should be close to a Dynojet center. go to <A HREF="http://www.dynojet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dynojet.com</A>  and find the closest tuning shop and run your car with an exhaust gas analyzer shoved up the pipes... they will be able to tell you if it really is rich or bad rings or whatever... and throwing more fuel at a car that is already running rich will just destroy your cat faster, make your car slower and make you mad! UNLESS... you have nitrous... you can never have to much gas with nitrous.. the more fuel you have the more torque you'll end up with.. thats why i have the bigger injectors in my car. but with much tuning it drives fine off the bottle, FINALLY...  you WILL pass emissions with the special chips.. ADS, JET and Hypertech both say you won't pass but as long as you have a cat and your EGR system is working right you'll do fine. under load and WOT does your car blow black smoke? that is unburnt fuel.. if it's blue/whiteish it's oil. BUT if you TACH up your car and then back off really fast your going to have a bit of white smoke cat or not... that is oil getting by the floating valves at or above 5500rpm. the stock valve springs aren't worth a crap after 5500 rpm.  just wondering why you think the car might be running rich. when you do get it on a dyno make sure you tell them that another Dynojet shop recommended you to them. Engineered Performance in Atlanta. The time usualy runs about $55-$85 dollars for 3-4 pulls. an all gear, and 2 or 3 3rd or 4th gear pulls. the computer knows what the gear ratios are and will compensate for the .24 under or over in 3rd or 4th compared to 1. before you spend money on a fuel pressure riser have you hooked the pressure guage to the car under load? mine hold over 100psi under nitrous and just over 80 under load with out nitrous. Don't throw parts at it... you might be wasting money.   <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 06-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||HYPTNOTiSE||06-19-2000||01:53 PM||||Hey got a few more things to add.<P>I think that it would be a good idea if you changed your fuel pump and got an adjustable fuel pressure regulator. I mean what the hell what's 200 bucks to make sure you're getting all the fuel you need.  Joe wynman the same guy who sells the chip that i use, has an adjustable fuel pressure regulator(AFPR) for i think 100 bucks, that's made of billet aluminum comes with all the internal parts needed, and has a trick dial on top that you can reach with your finger for adjustments without taking the upper intake plenum off. Very high quality along with every other of joe wynmans products i've seen.  Dont waste your money on a "Fiero" fuel pump.  GM uses the same pump in many differnt cars, the Camaro/firebirds use the same pump, so do Grand Nationals, and Eagle talon/Mitsu Eclipse.  They're a universal style and can be had through summit for 100 from granatelli motorsports. I'm running a 255lph fuel pump and a AFPR from joe wynman. Good stuff.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000008||HYPTNOTiSE||06-19-2000||02:04 PM||||Hey 1FST2M6,<P>If you want to start being able to afford driving your car everyday with your stock chip i know how you can do it. Goto SplitSec.com and look at the ARC-2 i just got one.  It allows full tunablity of the fuel management with the stock chip and you can run pretty much whatever injectors you want, you just tune to what specifics you want on you A/F meter. Basically that's what it is, A.R.C. Air/Fuel-Ratio-Calibrator.  Pretty sweet price on a new one is steep at around 5-6 hundred but i got mine used for 2 so keep your eyes peeled.<P>Later, <BR>Mike LeCompte||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FST2M6||06-19-2000||06:16 PM||||we found that looking around at the shop... the split sec is a good idea!  but i'm getting rid of the car and moving on to another.. and will be installing a LINK management system the first of sept. for demo at the NOPI show on SEPT. 16th and 17th. Thats a good idea for an upgrade for GT Bastard now!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  thanks for the idea but we found that out too late for me to really worry about.. Chris West had the same idea when i got my headers... the PMS module that we have to mess around with everything works pretty good but you can't drive around with the center counsel off all the time. EFI systems makes a E-PROM plug-in module for their hand held programming unit... the shop has the programming unit and for $60 i got the  adapter but that just gets us close and not really driveable... more like a band-aid than a fix. and unpractacle. SO you see this jeff?!? get a splitsec piggy back system! ||||reg||1
